🗺️ Mastering the "Massive World Map"
Handling a global-scale map requires specific optimization strategies from the start:

Use a Hybrid Data Approach: Combine raster tiles for broad overviews (zoom levels 0-10) and vector tiles for detailed, interactive views (zoom level 10+). This drastically reduces data transfer and speeds up rendering.

Cache Your Tiles: Cache already-rendered map tiles on the client side. This improves performance, reduces server load, and allows for some offline functionality.

Implement Spatial Indexing: For complex operations like figuring out if a point falls within a polygon, use spatial indexing systems like H3. This avoids computationally expensive "naive" searches and makes joins much faster.

Optimize User Interactions: Use techniques like debouncing map movements (zooming/panning) to prevent excessive event triggers and API calls. Auto-adjust the map view to the bounds of your data to avoid unnecessary reloading.

