You are correct: Leaflet is a free and open-source JavaScript library for creating interactive maps. It's important to distinguish between the Leaflet library itself, which is free software, and the map tiles you use with it, which may have associated costs.

🗺️ The Cost of Map Tiles
While Leaflet is free, it needs map tiles to display geography. You have several free and paid options:

Tile Provider	Key Information	Cost & Usage
OpenStreetMap (OSM)	Collaborative, open-source map of the world.	Free, but has a Tile Usage Policy for heavy use.
Mapbox	Commercial provider offering high-quality maps.	Paid service with a free tier; requires an API key.
Other Providers (Stamen, Thunderforest)	Various commercial and specialized providers.	Vary; often have free tiers for limited use.
🚀 How to Get Started with Leaflet
Here's the basic setup to get a free Leaflet map running quickly:

Include Leaflet Files: Add the library's CSS and JavaScript to your HTML head section. You can use a free CDN:

html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" crossorigin="" />
<script src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" crossorigin=""></script>
Create a Map Container: Place a <div> element with an ID in your HTML body and give it a height:

html
<div id="map" style="height: 400px;"></div>
Initialize the Map with Free Tiles: Use JavaScript to create the map and add a free tile layer, like OpenStreetMap:

javascript
var map = L.map('map').setView([51.505, -0.09], 13); // Coordinates for London

L.tileLayer('https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', {
    maxZoom: 19,
    attribution: '© <a href="http://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a>'
}).addTo(map);
💡 Key Considerations for Your Project
Check Tile Policies: For any tile provider, review their terms of service. OpenStreetMap, for example, should not be used for heavy traffic without permission.

Extend with Plugins: Leaflet's functionality can be expanded with many free plugins, such as Leaflet-Geoman for drawing and editing shapes.

